content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-24020; back pull-out design. [C01]",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 92 °C and rising. Bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface, and the applicable limits are normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reading is 22 °C above the normal limit, 12 °C above alarm and 2 °C above trip; the 90 °C trip limit therefore applies and the pump must be stopped now.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable vibration limits are Figure 3's HF-300 bearing-housing velocity zones in mm/s RMS. Numerically, the reported 4.0 mm/s falls in Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'; it is below the 4.5 mm/s RMS Zone C threshold for 'Restricted - plan maintenance' and below the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone D threshold for 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. This classification is provisional until the RMS and measurement-location details are confirmed. Zone B does not override the independent bearing-temperature trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The noisy bearing has no numerical noise limit in the evidence, but the manual's bearing-replacement criterion is met: both bearings must be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. The reported noise and 92 °C housing temperature independently meet that criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Condition monitoring requires vibration measurement on both bearing housings each week, with the highest reading classified. Only one report value is available, so compliance with that requirement and the highest overall vibration zone cannot be established.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is the leading suspected cause, but is not yet confirmed. It is a documented cause of high bearing temperature and high vibration, and the reported bearing noise/high temperature also triggers the manual's pair-replacement requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is the next suspected common cause because it is documented for both high bearing temperature and high vibration. Alignment must be checked, and laser alignment is required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing remains a documented possible cause of the high bearing temperature; check grease quantity. The evidence does not establish that it explains the bearing noise.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediately stop P-110 and do not continue operation on the basis of the Zone B vibration value: the drive-end housing is already above the 90 °C temperature trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, isolate and drain the pump. Preserve the documented seal-flush arrangement—Plan 11 from pump discharge—and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Troubleshoot and record the documented checks: check grease quantity, check alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller, and check NPSH. These checks are needed to distinguish bearing wear, over-greasing, misalignment and the other documented vibration causes rather than assuming a root cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For assembly access, use the back pull-out feature, which permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg and requires lifting equipment. Complete the bearing and impeller inspection while accessible.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair because of the reported noise and high temperature: drive-end bearing HF3-512, 6312-C3, and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510, 6310-C3, one of each. Do not replace only the drive-end bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened during the work, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket; the parts list requires replacement whenever the casing is opened. If the casing remains undisturbed, this conditional gasket requirement is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before closing the work, obtain the missing applicable bearing reassembly procedure and torque information rather than guessing; section 5.3 supplies the pair-replacement rule but no detailed bearing disassembly or torque steps, and the referenced Table 5 is not included in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On return to condition monitoring, measure bearing temperature on the housing surface and retain the limits of normal up to 70 °C, alarm 80 °C and trip 90 °C. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings weekly and classify the highest reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; required as one half of the mandatory bearing-pair replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing even though the report identifies the drive end.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Conditional casing gasket: required only if the casing is opened, because it must be replaced whenever the casing is opened; not required merely because a bearing is noisy or hot.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately: 92 °C exceeds the documented 90 °C bearing-housing trip. The vibration Zone B classification is not justification for continued operation.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before disassembly, following the manual's documented disassembly precaution.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; manual handling alone is not the documented method.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. The documented seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician, applicable after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. No combined crew-independent duration is calculated because the table lists different crew sizes for the two tasks.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list identifies component mechanical seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 prohibits that seal on applicable pumps and specifies HF3-450B instead. The bulletin was issued 14 March 2026 and applies to HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. P-110 is serial HF3-24020, so the serial-specific bulletin governs this asset: if seal replacement is separately required, do not fit HF3-450; use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B with no sleeve measurement and a gland-nut torque of 30 Nm, superseding the previous 25 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. This resolves the seal part/torque conflict but does not establish any need to replace the seal for the reported bearing fault.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The report does not state whether the 4.0 mm/s vibration value is RMS or on which bearing housing it was measured, and no second-housing reading is supplied. Confirm the measurement basis and measure both housings so the highest value can be classified. [C06, C07]",
    "Root cause remains unconfirmed: no grease-quantity finding, alignment measurement, bearing/impeller inspection result or NPSH data are provided. [C09]",
    "The correct grease type and required grease quantity are not included, although the troubleshooting table requires grease quantity to be checked. Obtain the applicable lubrication specification before adjusting or replenishing grease. [C09]",
    "Table 5 and the detailed section 5.3 bearing disassembly/reassembly and fastener-torque instructions are not present in the supplied evidence. Obtain the applicable documents before reassembly; do not assume the seal gland torque applies to other fasteners. [C10, C13]",
    "No seal leakage or other seal fault is reported, and the evidence does not state whether this bearing replacement will disturb the mechanical seal. Confirm that scope before adding seal work; if added, use the bulletin-mandated parts and torque and account for the separately listed seal-replacement labour of 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. [C09, C12, C13]",
    "Site-specific lockout/tagout, PPE and precautions for handling the hot housing are not described in the evidence. The supplied documents specify isolation/draining, lifting equipment and never running dry, but the remaining site safety arrangements must be confirmed. [C02, C10]"
  ]
}
